course: dictionary
lesson: 12830
title: Emulsion: when oil and water mix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An emulsion is a mixture of two liquids that do not usually mix, like oil and water. Shake them hard and you get tiny drops of one spread through the other. «Shake the oil and vinegar, and the dressing turns cloudy for a short time.» That cloudy mix is an emulsion, and it soon separates again.
explain: Emulsion has more than one meaning, so check the clues around it. «Ben painted his bedroom ceiling with white emulsion.» Here emulsion is paint, because painting and ceilings are the clues. «The old camera film had a light-sensitive emulsion on it.» Here it is the coating on the film.
explain: Ask yourself: are two liquids mixing, or is someone painting a wall? The clues tell you which meaning to use. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: An emulsion is a mixture of two liquids that do not usually mix.
fact: Mayonnaise, milk and salad dressing are all emulsions.
fact: In an emulsion, tiny drops of one liquid are spread through the other.
fact: In Britain, «emulsion» can also mean a water-based paint for walls and ceilings.
fact: Egg yolk can help hold an emulsion together, so the mixture stays mixed for longer.
exercise: «Shake the oil and vinegar, and you get an emulsion for a short time.» What is an emulsion? | A gas that rises into the sky | A solid rock that is hard to break | *A mixture of two liquids that do not usually mix | A sweet made from sugar and milk
exercise: «Mum bought a tin of white emulsion to paint the kitchen walls.» What is emulsion in this sentence? | A soft cushion | A cold drink | *Water-based paint for walls and ceilings | A kind of cake
exercise: Which of these is an emulsion? | Chalk | *Mayonnaise | Glass | Gravel
test: «The old film had a light-sensitive emulsion on it.» What does emulsion mean here? | A bright light | *The light-sensitive coating on photographic film | A pair of glasses | A kind of camera
test: «Egg yolk helps the oil and vinegar stay mixed in the dressing.» What kind of mixture is the dressing? | A solid that cannot be cut | A powder | *An emulsion | A gas
exam: «Dad mixed the oil and vinegar and shook the jar, making an emulsion.» What does emulsion mean in this sentence? | A paint for walls | *A mixture of two liquids that do not usually mix | A dish of hot soup | A kind of photo film
